{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat in The Hague is finally breaking, and I have taken the coach to Breda. I must confess, the journey was tedious, but the city holds a curiosity that arrested me. In the church, I viewed a tomb ascribed to Michelangelo. It is a strange, heavy composition: a count and his wife in alabaster rest upon a black slab, while four standing figures—Julius Caesar, Hannibal, and Regulus, among them—support a second slab above them.\n\nIt struck me as a perfect image of the ethical substance. The private individual, the \"I,\" is merely the foundation. It is only when supported by the great, universal forces of history and state that the life gains any true weight or permanence. Without those pillars, the individual is merely a stone in the dust. I think of you and the boys, holding the family together with such quiet strength. I am tired, but my mind is clear. I hope the news from the university is good.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080243,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":220,"prompt_tokens":943,"total_tokens":1163,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-VL3JXuTDj7oyf3oYmfywBN7DPfSANIve","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":943,"prompt_ms":1013.077,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0743128313891834,"prompt_per_second":930.8275678946418,"predicted_n":220,"predicted_ms":5217.02,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.822009132420092,"predicted_per_second":41.97798743343901}}